1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,150
CHAPTER 1 — THE WRONG CHIP

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:12,577
The name came from invidia, the Latin word for envy. And the first chip, in 1995, was called the NV1.

3
00:00:12,797 --> 00:00:20,105
It had a problem. It drew objects using curved surfaces. And the rest of the industry chose triangles.

4
00:00:20,325 --> 00:00:28,325
When Microsoft built its standard for Windows games, it built it around triangles. The NV1 was left on the wrong side.

5
00:00:28,545 --> 00:00:35,699
NVIDIA had a contract with Sega for the chip in its next console. But it was still using the same wrong technology.

6
00:00:36,549 --> 00:00:39,933
The company had enough cash left for about thirty days.
